    "If a reverse proxy in front of your Hermes server asks for a header of its own, add it here. It is sent with every request to this server's Dashboard and Hermes API, the WebSocket and Apple Watch included, and kept in the Keychain. Redde's own headers, such as the API key, take precedence." : {

    },
    "If the Dashboard or the Hermes API sits behind Pangolin, make a Link to its resource and paste its access token here: the token ID and token as id.token, or the link that has p_token= in it. Sent as P-Access-Token-Id / P-Access-Token on every request and WebSocket. One token is used for both when the other is empty. Treat it like a password." : {

    },
    "If the Hermes Dashboard sits behind Cloudflare Access instead of a tailnet, create a service token in Zero Trust and paste its ID and secret. Sent as CF-Access-Client-Id / -Secret on every request and WebSocket." : {

